Subject: [PATCH] t214: prepare BPMP, wake 51, GICv2 and SMP state for SC7

Apply after 0006-t214-windows-restart-entry.patch. Enabled only when
SWITCH_LITE_SC7=1 on T210B01.

- Require non-zero PMC_SCRATCH1/PMC_SCRATCH39 warmboot state, active-low
  GIC Group 1 INTID 118 (PMU_EXT) delivery, NX B01 PMC power-good/power-off
  timers, active-low PMC wake event 51, and BPMP MRQ_ENABLE_SUSPEND before
  committing PSCI CPU_SUSPEND(PSTATE_ID_SOC_POWERDN = 0x4000001B).
- Cancel MRQ_ENABLE_SUSPEND and downgrade cleanly to C7 when another CPU
  wakes before the last-CPU cluster lock completes.
- Save and restore non-secure GICv2 Group 1 banked CPU state across C7/CC6/SC7
  and global distributor SPIs, PMC interrupt polarity and SYSCTR0 across SC7.
- Re-initialize secondary CPU reset vectors (SB_AA64_RESET_LOW/HI), MC AHB
  redirection disable, FIQ routing, and wake C7-suspended secondary cores on
  SC7 exit while keeping CPU_OFF cores powered down.

References:
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/soc/tegra/pm-tegra210.c
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/soc/tegra/pmc.c
https://github.com/LineageOS/android_hardware_nintendo_arm-trusted-firmware/commit/85081cab2050051ea6e93206ef0f80bc0676e613

